# Text adventure — an M0 validation program (00 §33.1).
#
# Three rooms; you walk until you reach the treasure. Rooms are structures in
# a map keyed by name; the lamp-oil meter bounds the game. `use math for
# floor` brings in the module form the student layer owns.

use math for floor

structure room
    has name of type text
    has description of type text
    has north of type text

make halls equal to a map from "entrance" to a room with name "entrance" and description "a dusty entrance hall" and north "library", "library" to a room with name "library" and description "shelves and one creaky ladder" and north "vault", "vault" to a room with name "vault" and description "a locked iron door" and north ""

make changing room here equal to "entrance"
make changing lamp oil equal to 10
make changing treasure found equal to false

repeat while treasure found is equal to false
    make here equal to halls at room here
    say "you are in the {name of here} — {description of here}"
    decrease lamp oil by 1
    if lamp oil is at most 0
        say "your lamp goes out. the dark wins."
        stop
    make move equal to ask "go north, or look? "
    if move is equal to "north"
        make going north equal to north of here
        if going north is equal to ""
            say "there is no door that way."
        otherwise if going north is equal to "vault"
            say "the vault! the treasure is yours."
            set treasure found to true
        otherwise
            set room here to going north
    otherwise if move is equal to "look"
        say "you see dust, and a door north."
    otherwise
        say "you cannot do that."

say "the end."
